Presidential elections were held in the [[Republic of Montenegro (1992–2006)|Republic of Montenegro]] on 22 December 2002.<ref name=AC>[http://psephos.adam-carr.net/countries/m/montenegro/montenegropres.txt Republic of Montenegro Presidential Election of 2002-2003] Adam Carr</ref>

==Background==
The elections were boycotted by the opposition [[Socialist People's Party of Montenegro|Socialist People's Party]], who accused the ruling [[Democratic Party of Socialists of Montenegro|Democratic Party of Socialists]] of pressurising civil servants to vote for Vujanović.<ref name=BBC/> The elections were also overshadowed by the arrest of Deputy State Attorney Zoran Piperović for connections with human trafficking and forced prostitution.<ref name=BBC>[https://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/europe/2598415.stm Montenegro vote ruled invalid] BBC News, 23 December 2003</ref>

==Results==
Although Dragan Hajduković was a member of the [[Greens of Montenegro]], he ran as an independent.

