==Aftermath==
Although [[Filip Vujanović]] won the election with 86% of the vote, turnout was less than the required 50%, so the election was declared invalid.<ref name=AC/> [[February 2003 Montenegrin presidential election|Fresh elections]] were held in February 2003, which were also invalidated, and then again in [[May 2003 Montenegrin presidential election|May]] when the turnout rule was abolished.

